WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.720 --> 00:00:02.260
What do taxis,

00:00:02.260 --> 00:00:03.460
playing cards,

00:00:03.460 --> 00:00:04.520
love hotels,

00:00:04.520 --> 00:00:06.750
and Game Boys have in common?

00:00:06.750 --> 00:00:10.760
At one point, they were all a Nintendo venture.

00:00:10.770 --> 00:00:16.430
These products are among the mega-hits and
mega-flops in Nintendo’s 130 year history.

00:00:16.430 --> 00:00:21.010
Whenever the end was near, they bounced back
with an innovative, company-saving product.

00:00:21.010 --> 00:00:26.500
And their secret to modern success: great
games with classic characters.

00:00:26.500 --> 00:00:32.040
This is how Nintendo periodically turned reports
of its imminent demise into Nintendo mania.

00:00:35.920 --> 00:00:39.900
From 2010 to 2015, Nintendo was in trouble.

00:00:39.900 --> 00:00:45.040
Its most recent major console, the Wii U,
was considered a flop next to its rivals.

00:00:45.040 --> 00:00:48.500
Profits were tumbling, and its stock price
was near a low.

00:00:48.500 --> 00:00:53.350
Worse still, some analysts saw the surging
popularity of mobile smartphone games as

00:00:53.350 --> 00:00:57.500
a major threat to Nintendo’s cash cow: its
portable gaming systems.

00:00:57.500 --> 00:01:03.560
Another major blow came in July 2015 with
the death of the company’s president, Satoru Iwata.

00:01:04.610 --> 00:01:07.100
But then, Nintendo’s fortune suddenly reversed.

00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:12.610
In late 2016, it released a mobile smartphone
game, the wildly popular Super Mario Run,

00:01:12.610 --> 00:01:18.240
and capitalized on fan nostalgia with the
limited edition NES Classic.

00:01:18.240 --> 00:01:23.310
Then in March 2017, the company released the
long-awaited Nintendo Switch, which became

00:01:23.310 --> 00:01:24.300
an instant hit.

00:01:24.300 --> 00:01:27.940
It's just a very sleek and nicely

00:01:27.940 --> 00:01:31.530
designed and pleasing hardware to have

00:01:31.530 --> 00:01:33.390
in your hands.

00:01:33.390 --> 00:01:38.670
But that said, it really comes down to the
games and they had an incredibly strong lineup

00:01:38.670 --> 00:01:40.450
of games from the start.

00:01:40.450 --> 00:01:44.830
With the help of these reimagined classics,
Nintendo sold more than 20 million units in

00:01:44.830 --> 00:01:48.940
the first two years and it’s now become the
fastest selling console in U.S. history.

00:01:48.940 --> 00:01:57.040
They have this kind of Disney-like
ability to introduce their characters in one

00:01:57.040 --> 00:02:02.880
format and then maybe your interest in their
products fades away a little bit and then

00:02:02.880 --> 00:02:08.400
years later they'll reintroduce those same
characters again with a new product.

00:02:08.400 --> 00:02:13.300
The Switch was hardly the first time Nintendo had pivoted successfully to a new type of entertainment.

00:02:15.380 --> 00:02:20.720
Nintendo began in Kyoto in 1889 with hand
painted playing cards called "hanafuda"

00:02:20.720 --> 00:02:22.920
or "flower cards".

00:02:22.920 --> 00:02:28.280
Because western style playing cards were banned,
Japanese gangsters, called “Yakuza” favored

00:02:28.280 --> 00:02:30.310
these in their illegal gambling parlours.

00:02:30.310 --> 00:02:32.960
And Nintendo made a killing.

00:02:32.960 --> 00:02:39.720
They made every kind of playing card imaginable
until 1963, dubbed “Nintendo’s experimental years.”

00:02:39.720 --> 00:02:44.540
During this time they did everything from
food, taxis, and love hotels, before circling

00:02:44.540 --> 00:02:46.440
back to toys.

00:02:46.440 --> 00:02:53.300
There was even a self made extending arm - called
the Ultra Hand, The Love Tester, Ultra Machine,

00:02:53.300 --> 00:02:58.520
and even a laser clay shooting system that
would later morph into NES’s classic Duck Hunt.

00:02:58.520 --> 00:03:02.560
The success of some of these toys cemented
their place as a toy maker, leading them into

00:03:02.560 --> 00:03:04.230
the gaming industry.

00:03:04.230 --> 00:03:09.300
Nintendo only started developing home gaming
consoles about 35 years ago - with the introduction

00:03:09.300 --> 00:03:13.709
of the Famicom in Japan and Nintendo Entertainment
System in the U.S.

00:03:13.709 --> 00:03:16.500
Their timing however, couldn’t have been
worse.

00:03:18.180 --> 00:03:19.940
The gaming industry was crashing.

00:03:19.940 --> 00:03:24.100
There were too many consoles and too many
terrible third party games.

00:03:26.540 --> 00:03:29.060
But Nintendo succeeded where others didn’t.

00:03:29.069 --> 00:03:33.480
They bundled a hit game called Super Mario
Brothers created by visionary game designer

00:03:33.480 --> 00:03:34.820
Shigeru Miyamoto.

00:03:34.820 --> 00:03:39.629
To date, this game has sold over 40 million
copies worldwide, holding the record for

00:03:39.629 --> 00:03:41.610
a full 18 years.

00:03:41.610 --> 00:03:47.459
Miyamoto, who joined Nintendo in 1977, would
go on to design other hits like Zelda, Mario

00:03:47.459 --> 00:03:48.470
Kart, and Starfox.

00:03:48.470 --> 00:03:54.569
“I like making games so much that
I would like to do it for free.”

00:03:54.569 --> 00:04:00.100
And each new gaming console over the next
few decades had the key hit games to go with it:

00:04:00.100 --> 00:04:03.320
The Game Boy had Tetris and Kirby’s Dreamland.

00:04:03.320 --> 00:04:07.599
The Super Nintendo had Super Mario World and
Donkey Kong Country.

00:04:07.600 --> 00:04:11.900
And the N64 had Mario Kart, Goldeneye and
Zelda: Ocarina of Time.

00:04:11.900 --> 00:04:17.860
They now have people like you and me who grew up playing with games

00:04:17.860 --> 00:04:21.920
with Mario and Link in the case of Zelda.

00:04:21.920 --> 00:04:25.480
It's pleasing to pass along those characters
to your own children

00:04:25.490 --> 00:04:29.139
But, they had their share of flops as well.

00:04:29.139 --> 00:04:34.479
Like...the Virtual Boy: a headset that allowed
the user to play games in virtual reality.

00:04:34.479 --> 00:04:36.880
The Game Cube was also less than successful.

00:04:36.880 --> 00:04:44.580
And while 2018 was the best year in over a
decade - the forecast is once again not so positive.

00:04:44.580 --> 00:04:49.900
In September of 2018, more than a decade after
rivals Sony and Microsoft, Nintendo debuted

00:04:49.900 --> 00:04:53.440
its first online subscription service.

00:04:53.440 --> 00:04:55.290
But the reviews haven’t been great.

00:04:55.290 --> 00:05:00.350
Gamers complain that Nintendo’s platform
lacks must-have features like in-game chat.

00:05:00.350 --> 00:05:04.280
They say it’s susceptible to cheating and
get frustrated with its connectivity issues.

00:05:04.280 --> 00:05:11.540
They seem to manage, whether it was
the Wii or Game Boy or the Switch most recently.

00:05:11.540 --> 00:05:16.460
They do seem to come back just when people
have written them off, and they do seem to

00:05:16.460 --> 00:05:19.880
come up with these new things to push things
forward.

00:05:19.880 --> 00:05:26.490
So it'll be interesting to see how they react
to this shift to online multiplayer games.

00:05:26.490 --> 00:05:31.000
They'll probably come up with something new
in that arena too if you give them enough time.

00:05:31.000 --> 00:05:35.700
After all, it wouldn’t be the first time
Nintendo reinvented itself.

